              "text": "[Document context]\nTitle: Reject unsupported batch request features before execution\nSource: agent-memory\nPath: /memory/semantic_memory/reject-unsupported-batch-request-features-before-execution-a4107859.md\nWorkspace: agent-memory\nTeam: Marcus Reed\n\n# Reject unsupported batch request features before execution\n\nMemory type: semantic_memory\nRecorded: 2026-08-16T08:10:39.907424+00:00\nConfidence: 0.99\nOwner: Marcus Reed\nTags: vllm, batch-chat, api-compatibility, validation, fail-closed\n\n## Summary\n\nFor vLLM batch chat, any request feature the endpoint cannot honor (notably streaming and tools in the pinned #50026 contract) must be rejected during request-model validation with a parameter-specific client error. Do not silently drop fields or allow streaming delta output into a collector designed for final full outputs. Preserve explicitly supported values such as stream=False.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- /knowledge/company/sources/github_public/vllm-project/vllm/issues/50026.json\n- /knowledge/company/sources/slack/eng-platform/1749994321-transport-compatibility-and-proto-validation.json\n- /code/vllm/vllm/entrypoints/openai/chat_completion/protocol.py\n- /code/vllm/tests/entrypoints/openai/chat_completion/test_chat_error.py\n- /artifacts/reviews/vllm-50026.md",
